                                "sense_id": "639777d3-bfda-393e-af43-4fdec03bd3a3",
                                "text": "[…] thereby causing the rowiness or pattern-like appearance, which is completely obviated by the present contrivance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "566e5592-2846-4540-945e-a32023c7f63b",
                                "sense_id": "639777d3-bfda-393e-af43-4fdec03bd3a3",
                                "text": "In Mr. Heath's machine […] is the means by which he obtains lines not only varied in themselves, but differing from each other so as to avoid rowiness, and thus to produce, it is presumed, a near resemblance to hand-ruling, retaining, at the same time, the perfect equality of distance between the lines and uniformity of strength characteristic of machine-ruling."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2071cfa-b9e6-441d-83b0-c4190e3e2e42",
                                "sense_id": "639777d3-bfda-393e-af43-4fdec03bd3a3",
                                "text": "[…] and often through rowiness and being uneven he has to dye it again, a loss the skein dyer seldom has to complain of."
                            }
                        ]
